# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows. With CRLF, bash reads the
# shebang line as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` and fails with a bad-interpreter
# error, or splits a heredoc on the stray carriage return. This repo is
# developed on Windows, so the default checkout would otherwise convert them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Every text file is checked out LF, whatever core.autocrlf says. The index
# has always been LF; the churn was working copies checked out CRLF while
# tools (gleam format, node, the harness) wrote LF back, so git listed
# untouched files as modified with zero changed lines. Binary detection is
# left to git (`auto`).
* text=auto eol=lf
